<title>PORTUGAL: NATO-Ukraine set to agree security pact.</title>
<headline>NATO-Ukraine set to agree security pact.</headline>
<dateline>SINTRA, Portugal 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>NATO and Ukraine have agreed the outlines of a security pact, similar to one NATO leaders signed earlier this week with Russia, and will formally adopt it later on Thursday, NATO diplomats said.</p>
<p>The accord, which gives Ukraine the right to call for &quot;consultations&quot; with NATO states if it feels threatened, is intended to give the huge former Soviet republic a more weighty relationship than that of most partnership countries.</p>
</text>
